# Consent Form Rules

Consent forms MUST be created as a **multiple checkbox question**, not radio buttons or a single yes/no item.

## Required Behaviour

- Each consent statement must appear as a separate checkbox.
- Participants must tick ALL required consent boxes before continuing.
- Consent forms should use hard validation.
- The question name must include `_FORCE`.

Example:

```text
consent_FORCE
```

## SurveyJS Consent Structure

Use a checkbox question with all consent items listed as choices.

Example:

```json
{
  "type": "checkbox",
  "name": "consent_FORCE",
  "title": "Consent Form",
  "description": "Please tick each box to confirm your consent.",
  "isRequired": true,
  "validators": [
    {
      "type": "answercount",
      "minCount": 5,
      "text": "You must tick all consent boxes to continue."
    }
  ],
  "choices": [
    {
      "value": "read_information",
      "text": "I confirm that I have read and understood the participant information sheet."
    },
    {
      "value": "voluntary",
      "text": "I understand that participation is voluntary."
    },
    {
      "value": "withdraw",
      "text": "I understand that I can withdraw within the stated withdrawal period."
    },
    {
      "value": "data_use",
      "text": "I understand how my data will be stored and used."
    },
    {
      "value": "agree",
      "text": "I agree to take part in this study."
    }
  ]
}
```

## Important Rule

The `minCount` MUST match the number of required consent items.

Examples:

- 5 consent items = `"minCount": 5`
- 7 consent items = `"minCount": 7`

Do NOT use a single consent checkbox unless explicitly requested.

